What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/numa_scan_size_mb
Date:		July 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write size, in megabytes, of the virtual address range
		processed by each normal automatic NUMA-balancing scan. The value
		must be non-zero. Writes require CAP_SYS_ADMIN.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/numa_scan_period_min_ms
Date:		July 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write lower bound, in milliseconds, for the adaptive normal
		NUMA-balancing scan period. The value must be non-zero. Writes
		require CAP_SYS_ADMIN.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/numa_scan_period_max_ms
Date:		July 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write upper bound, in milliseconds, for the adaptive normal
		NUMA-balancing scan period. The value must be non-zero. Writes
		require CAP_SYS_ADMIN.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/numa_scan_delay_ms
Date:		July 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write initial delay, in milliseconds, before normal automatic
		NUMA balancing begins scanning a task. Zero starts scanning without
		an initial delay. Writes require CAP_SYS_ADMIN.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/local_fault_rate
Date:		May 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write percentage controlling local-tier refault sampling.
		Zero disables the local sampler. Values from 1 through 100 select
		base-page PFNs at the requested rate.

		The local sampler can run while kernel.numa_balancing is zero.
		It installs NUMA protection probes but does not enable migration.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/local_fault_scan_period_ms
Date:		May 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write local-tier sampling period in milliseconds. The value
		must be non-zero.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/local_fault_scan_size_mb
Date:		May 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write maximum amount of local-tier memory, in megabytes, for
		which probes are installed during one sampler invocation. The value
		must be non-zero. The default is 64 megabytes.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/local_fault_window
Date:		May 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write sampling-window sequence. Reading returns the current
		sequence. Writing a non-zero integer advances the sequence. Local
		and remote KLL sketches are reset lazily when their first sample for
		the new sequence arrives.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/remote_scan_cycles
Date:		July 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-only cumulative count of completed normal NUMA address-space
		scan passes that installed at least one remote-tier access-time
		probe. A controller can use changes in this counter to align a
		sampling window with remote scan progress.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/fault_latency_quantiles
Date:		July 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-only weighted-KLL snapshot for the current sampling window.
		All values in one read come from the same copied sketch snapshot.
		The quantile_snapshot_v4 schema contains:

		schema
		window_seq
		algorithm
		value_source
		local_total
		remote_total
		local_q75_ns
		remote_query_rank_ppm
		remote_query_q_ns
		remote_query_valid
		remote_cdf_lt_local_q75_ppm
		remote_cdf_le_local_q75_ppm

		The totals are page-weighted sample counts. local_q75_ns is zero
		when there are no local samples. The CDF fields are integer parts
		per million in [0, 1000000], evaluated at local_q75_ns. The _lt_
		field excludes remote samples equal to local P75; the _le_ field
		includes them.

		remote_query_rank_ppm echoes the value of remote_quantile_rank_ppm
		captured at the start of this read. When that rank is in [1, 1000000]
		and the copied remote sketch is nonempty, remote_query_valid is one
		and remote_query_q_ns is the smallest latency whose inclusive remote
		CDF reaches that rank. Otherwise remote_query_valid and
		remote_query_q_ns are zero. A valid quantile can itself be zero, so
		consumers must check remote_query_valid rather than using the
		quantile value as a validity test.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/remote_quantile_rank_ppm
Date:		July 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write remote weighted-KLL query rank in integer parts per
		million. Values in [1, 1000000] select the inverse inclusive-CDF
		quantile returned by fault_latency_quantiles. Zero disables the
		query. Other values are rejected. Writing this query parameter does
		not advance the sampling window or change the sampling policy.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/migration_enabled
Date:		July 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write Boolean gate for NUMA-balancing page migration. Zero
		keeps normal NUMA scanning, protection faults, and latency sampling
		active while rejecting page moves. One permits migrations selected
		by the active NUMA-balancing mode.
